#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065440 :tutorial/content "When we want to multiply two binomials, we take each term of the first binomial and multiply it by the second binomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\nFor example, to multiply $({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})$ and $(x + 2)$, we multiply ${\\color{blue}{x}}$ and $(x + 2)$, and then we add this to the product of ${\\color{red}{3}}$ and $(x+2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} ({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})(x + 2) \\\\[5pt] &= {\\color{blue}{x}}(x + 2) + {\\color{red}{3}}(x + 2) \\\\[5pt] &= x^2 + 2x + 3x + 6 \\\\[5pt] &= x^2 + 5x + 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "0cea50d1-e4ce-511f-821f-0e5e04b6eca1" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8877 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
